<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gilbert de Clare, 1st Earl of Pembroke</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1100–1148</span> · Also known as Gilbert fitz Gilbert de Clare</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humphrey-gilbert">Gilbert</a> de Clare, 1st Earl of Pembroke, was an Anglo-Norman baron created Earl of Pembroke by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-king-of-england">King Stephen</a> in 1138, giving the lordship palatine powers. He supported Stephen during the Anarchy. His son Richard de Clare, known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-de-clare-2nd-earl-of-pembroke">Strongbow</a>, led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-norman-invasion-of-ireland">Anglo-Norman invasion of Ireland</a> in 1170.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gilbert-de-clare-1st-earl-of-pembroke.jpg" alt="Gilbert de Clare, 1st Earl of Pembroke" width="320" height="641" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Horace Round · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_Gilbert_Fitz_Gilbert_de_Clare,_Earl_of_Pembroke.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
